cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Cadence: an SLO-aware LLM inference gateway"
message: "If you use this software or its methodology in your work, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Benamour
    given-names: Aymen Abderrahim
repository-code: "https://github.com/BAAAAR19/Cadence"
abstract: >-
  Cadence is an OpenAI-compatible LLM inference gateway combining continuous
  batching, paged KV-cache management, radix prefix reuse, and conformal
  admission control. Its open-loop benchmark measures goodput and tail latency
  under overload, while a C++17 core is differentially tested against Python
  reference implementations.
keywords:
  - llm-inference
  - continuous-batching
  - conformal-prediction
  - admission-control
  - systems
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-09-10"
